From bf005e828a2806dd4dca9fade8c5ed390ac52d32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ejc3 <ejc3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:58:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] KVM: x86: keep a pending PV kick across an async page-ready
 completion

kvm_arch_async_page_present() makes the vCPU runnable through
kvm_set_mp_state(), and since commit e9cb61055fee ("KVM: x86: Clear
pv_unhalted on all transitions to KVM_MP_STATE_RUNNABLE") that helper also
clears vcpu->arch.pv.pv_unhalted. A page-ready completion is delivered to
a vCPU that is usually already runnable, so here the helper is not a
wake-up from HLT: it erases a PV kick (KVM_HC_KICK_CPU) that has not been
consumed yet. The guest need not have enabled async page faults: without
them KVM halts the vCPU artificially and completes through the same
function.

A PV spinlock waiter checks the lock and then executes HLT, with
interrupts off when the lock is taken from interrupt context. If the
holder releases the lock and kicks the waiter between the check and the
HLT, the kick is recorded in pv_unhalted and the HLT must not block. When
a page-ready completion for the waiter is handled in that window the
kick is lost, the HLT blocks, and with interrupts off nothing but an NMI
wakes the vCPU. Every other CPU that then sends it an IPI and waits
(a TLB flush in smp_call_function_many_cond(), for example) spins for
ever: the guest reports soft lockups and stops.

Seen on a 7.3.3 host with 6.18.60 guests restored from a snapshot through
userfaultfd (many async page faults right after the restore) while the
host is oversubscribed: 15 of 900 two-vCPU guests. A trace of one:

  vcpu0 kvm_hypercall       nr 0x5 a0 0x0 a1 0x1      (KVM_HC_KICK_CPU)
  vcpu0 kvm_apic_accept_irq apicid 1 vec 0 (Res3|edge)
  vcpu1 kvm_async_pf_ready  token 0xe9001 gva 0x4e4cd20
  vcpu1 kvm_exit            reason HLT
  (no kvm_vcpu_wakeup for vcpu1 until the guest's watchdog sends an NMI)

Set the state directly, as the function did before the helper existed, so
the kick survives. No other caller of kvm_set_mp_state() is changed.

Fixes: e9cb61055fee ("KVM: x86: Clear pv_unhalted on all transitions to KVM_MP_STATE_RUNNABLE")
---
 arch/x86/kvm/x86.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kvm/x86.c b/arch/x86/kvm/x86.c
index c76498d..843a567 100644
--- a/arch/x86/kvm/x86.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/x86.c
@@ -10601,7 +10601,14 @@ void kvm_arch_async_page_present(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu,
 	}
 
 	vcpu->arch.apf.halted = false;
-	kvm_set_mp_state(vcpu, KVM_MP_STATE_RUNNABLE);
+	/*
+	 * Not kvm_set_mp_state(): that also clears pv_unhalted, and a page-ready
+	 * completion is not the wake-up a PV kick is waiting to deliver.  A vCPU
+	 * kicked between its last check of a PV spinlock and its HLT is still
+	 * RUNNABLE here; clearing the kick lets that HLT block with interrupts
+	 * off, and nothing but an NMI wakes it.
+	 */
+	vcpu->arch.mp_state = KVM_MP_STATE_RUNNABLE;
 }
 
 void kvm_arch_async_page_present_queued(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu)
-- 
2.43.0

